 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+Eviction uses 2Q, which separates sheets screened once from sheets editors return to, so a long sequential screening cannot evict a working set of comparison sheets. A probationary queue (A1) holds sheets rendered but not yet reused; a main queue (Am) holds sheets requested more than once. A newly completed sheet is admitted at the MRU end of A1. A cache hit on a sheet in A1 promotes it to the MRU end of Am; a cache hit on a sheet already in Am moves it to the MRU end of Am. When admission requires eviction, evict from the LRU end of A1 first, and only evict from the LRU end of Am once A1 is empty. The split of the 12 GiB budget between A1 and Am is a tunable parameter, not yet fixed (see Open Questions & Future Decisions). Both queues and the size split are private bookkeeping of this worker; no other node observes or depends on them, and the eviction policy does not change the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (probationary queue A1 + main queue Am) | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | See [decisions/eviction-policy.md](decisions/eviction-policy.md). |
+
